        "side": "new",
        "severity": "low",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Close does not free memzones, hw->mz or peer_mw_size",
        "explanation": "dev_close unregisters interrupts but never frees the memory-window memzones, hw->mz or hw->peer_mw_size. These resources leak once the device is released.",
        "suggestion": "Call rte_memzone_free on each hw->mz[i], then rte_free hw->mz and hw->peer_mw_size.",
